      "type": "raw",
      "heading": "How new code goes live.",
      "html": "<p class=\"site-words\">Changes are built and tried on a separate test system first. Code reaches the live product only through a step the founder starts with an explicit word, and from anywhere except one chat app, a one-time code from his authenticator app as well. The code is checked in software, each code works once, and five wrong codes in an hour lock it. An automated task or an AI assistant cannot start it. If a check fails after going live, the previous version is put back automatically, and the database is copied first.</p>"
